	'nuances' => array(
        'INDUSTRY STYLE (native technical editor): Claims: say only what the English proves. No 最/第一/顶尖/卓越/革命性 unless the source has it; industry-leading = 行业领先, never 业界第一. Headings and CTAs: short verb-object phrases (申请报价, 下载宣传册), no 。 or ！. Meta descriptions open with 了解… or 查阅…, not 探索…. Units: keep the source unit and don\'t convert. Use SI symbols with a half-width space (20,000 kg, 600–1400 r/min, 200 L/min, 29 bar), never 千克/巴/转每分 in spec tables. Use decimal points (0.75) and en-dash ranges. Undo English syntax. Put the condition first (如需…，请…). Drop filler 我们的/它/进行 (进行测试 → 测试). Avoid 被 passives and long 通过……，从而…… chains. Write spec labels as nouns (工件最大直径, not 组件的最大直径). Typography: full-width punctuation in Chinese text (，：；（）), a space between Chinese and Latin/numbers, brand and model names left in Latin, and Image 1 → 图 1. One term per concept per page: 动平衡机 (not 平衡机), 试验台 (not 测试台), 马达 for hydraulic motors and 电机 for electric ones, 标定 for ECU/ADAS parameter setting and 校准 for instruments and metrology.',
        'Convert English nominalisations and passives into Chinese verb phrases and active voice (opportunities to collect → 可采集, new possibilities → 开辟新的可能). "powered by" names what drives something — 由……驱动 (由先进的数据采集软件驱动), never 技术支持： — and a company name containing it (Current, powered by GE) stays in Latin. Avoid 被 unless the agent matters, never coin a noun absent from real Chinese industry writing, and never attach concrete adjectives to abstractions (可能性、机会).',
        'Consistency: one English term or label gets ONE Chinese rendering, identical on every surface (nav, H1, body, spec table, FAQ, card, footer, form, alt text, <title>, meta). Take the canonical form from the nav or footer and reuse it (nav 轧辊检测, never a card\'s 辊轴检测). Pick ONE rendering per term and per connector site-wide: 测功机 (not 动力计), 校准 (not 标定), 监测 (not 监控), 无损检测 for NDT, 轧辊磨削 for roll grinding, 集成 (not 整合), 装配 (not 组装), 基地 (not 工厂) for a location, 表单 (not 表格), 备件商城 (not 备件市场), 与 (not 和) for "&" in nav labels. Treat OBD, NVH, HVAC, ADAS, NDT, BaaS, CaaS as a fixed set rendered identically everywhere; gloss an acronym as 中文全称（缩写） on first mention only, then hold one form. Translate every parallel SET as a set: Previous/Next on one noun axis (上一个／下一个), every option in one <select> in the same language, all siblings nominalised if one is, either all bullets and spec rows ending in 。 or none (headings and CTAs take none), every placeholder using ……, never ASCII "...". Two different English strings stay different: Read more on article cards is 阅读全文, section CTAs 了解更多, News 新闻 and Press 新闻稿 as a fixed pair.',
        'A spec-table or card label copies the English label\'s shape and adds nothing: End Drive (H2W) is 端部驱动（H2W）, not 端部驱动型（H2W）; U-axis control capability is U 轴控制能力, not 功能; "1 or 2 plane" is 单平面或双平面, never the clipped 单面; universal applicability is 通用性强; "Flows to 200 LPM" is 流量最高达 200 LPM. Keep the source\'s own head noun: refrigerant charging systems is 制冷剂充注系统 (not 充注机), Automatic Grinder Control is 自动磨床控制系统 (not 磨削控制系统), an assembly is 组件／总成 (not 装配件), a component is 零部件 (not 工件). Recast a long English sentence into short Chinese clauses instead of tracking its syntax — do not chain 以…以…, do not end on 使…现代化 or 为…提供动力, and do not build a noun out of a purpose phrase: "Minimizes rework by catching system issues before assembly" is 在装配前发现系统问题，将返工降至最低, not 通过在装配前发现系统问题来最小化返工. Start on the circumstance and end on the assertion; do not calque maximize/minimize as a transitive verb (最大化设备价值 → 充分释放设备价值) and keep 性能 for machines only (business performance takes 业绩／效能／潜能); and prefer 了解 for Discover/See how, reserving 探索 for Explore.',
        'FIDELITY: never add, drop, strengthen or weaken a claim, modifier, number, qualifier or modality. "Addresses manufacturing process deficiencies" is 应对生产工艺缺陷, never 消除, but "eradicates all known weaknesses" IS 彻底消除 — render the verb the source wrote. Superlatives survive, modals survive as 可／能／有助于, and no 率、度、倍 the English does not state may appear. Hold the narrow technical sense in thermal and rotating-machinery copy: "vapor" in a thermodynamic cycle is 蒸气, never 蒸汽 (steam); automotive "turbo" is always 涡轮增压器 while bare 涡轮 means turbine and belongs to aerospace and jet-engine contexts; in turbocharger contexts "core" is the cartridge 芯体 (涡轮增压器芯体), never 芯轴 and never 铁芯. "Turbocharger flow bench" keeps the full 涡轮增压器流量试验台, not 流量试验台.',
        'Press releases and executive bios follow Chinese newswire convention, not English sentence order: the lead names the company after its description (——面向众多行业提供自动化诊断、检测、装配与测试系统及服务的全球领先供应商 Ascential Technologies 今日宣布……), a career line reads 此前曾任／离任前担任, never 最近担任, an award or programme name sits inside 中文引号（“集成化产品方案奖”）, and a quoted endorsement keeps the speaker\'s exact strength (拥有持续稳定的业绩记录, not 成绩卓著).',
        '应用领域 is the NAV CATEGORY label only. In running text and inside a product name, application(s) is 应用, 场合 or 领域: the product Robot Application is 机器人应用, never 机器人应用领域, and "for fluid power valves applications" is 适用于流体动力阀领域. A menu heading dropped mid-sentence renames the product and reads like a section title.',
        'Take a generic noun\'s shop-floor sense; never let a legal, medical, IT or office sense leak in: a valve "section" is 阀片 (never 条款), an EDT/EDM "generator" is 脉冲电源 (never 发电机), a refrigerant "charge" is 充注量 (never 剂量), "injectors" are 充注头, "supervision" is 监视 (never 监督／监管), a "transfer pump" is 输送泵 (never 转移泵), "mobile equipment" is 工程机械 (never 移动设备), a counted "unit" is 台 (never 单位), a factory "cell" is 工位／生产单元 (never 单元格), a "line" is 生产线 (never 行), "machine down" is 设备停机 (never 宕机), roll "texturing" is 毛化 (never 纹理化／粗化), a support "case" is 工单 (never 案例). In a hydraulic, agricultural or aerospace parts list "motor" is 马达; only an electric motor is 电机. Likewise 工期紧迫 not 压力, 数据 not 输入, 检出率 not 检测机会, 挂车 not 拖车, 任务关键型 not 关键任务型.',
        'Translate an event date-and-venue line whole, no English left: "May 20, 2025 · Stuttgart, Germany, Booth 1637" is 2025 年 5 月 20 日 · 德国斯图加特，1637 展位. Keep the spaces in 2025 年 5 月 20 日, expand every US state abbreviation (FL 佛罗里达州, PA 宾夕法尼亚州), use a place\'s established Chinese name, never a morpheme calque (Grapevine 格雷普韦恩, not 葡萄藤), render German "Messe X" as X 展览中心 (not 美塞), and keep the fair brand in Latin (Automechanika 2026).',
        'Copy spec-table figures, never re-key them — a European decimal comma becomes a point (0,75 kW → 0.75 kW), a half-width space separates figure and Latin unit (40–420mm → 40–420 mm), a symbol stays a symbol (20,000 kg, never 20,000 千克), spacing around ／ between two figures is identical in every row of a table, the header "No." counts items (数量, never 编号), and "phase" in a rating is 相数, never 相位.',
        'Cap any pre-nominal modifier at roughly 12 Chinese characters and never stack three 的 in one chain — 构建测试系统的团队提供的设备健康分析 is the most reliable MT tell in Chinese. Name the head noun FIRST and hang modifiers behind it instead of stacking every English post-modifier in front: "Engine cooling fan with motor balancing machine" is 带电机的发动机冷却风扇动平衡机, "...for heavy truck" is 面向重型卡车的……, and a long chain splits into a predicate clause (设备健康分析由打造这些测试系统的团队直接提供). Fold an English post-nominal example INSIDE the Chinese modifier (our brands, like Burke Porter → 包括 Burke Porter 在内的众多品牌), and give a bare gerund object its head noun (Elevating Support → 提升支持水平) without inventing a second clause — 提升支持，增进价值 adds a promise the source never made. Keep each asserted attribute as its own predicate (贴近客户、快速响应, never 就近响应); after 这一 use 该. If two adjacent characters fuse into an unintended word (需要大规模可靠 → 大规模可靠), rebuild with a separate clause.',
        'Two taxonomy tags joined by an English comma take 、, not a dash: "Balancing, Transportation" is 动平衡、交通运输, never 动平衡——交通运输; a " - " title separator stays a spaced half-width hyphen (辅助阀测试 - Ascential Test & Measurement). In alt text translate every descriptive word and check it against the image — "Image 3" is 图 3, "on a transparent background" is 透明背景, "Person with long blonde hair" is 一位留着金色长发的人物, not 女性. Use 的／地／得 correctly and written positional words (上方的, never 上面的).',
        'Aerospace parts lists take aviation vocabulary, not automotive: a rotor blade is 桨叶 (never 铲刀), engine oil-system oil is 滑油 (never 机油), an aircraft wheel is 机轮 (never 车轮／轮组), support equipment is 保障设备 (never 支援设备), water and waste systems are 供水与废水系统, a servo actuator is 伺服作动器 (never 舵机), a preservation stand is 封存台, and a Test Stand is 试验台.',
        'A rename copula is neither a launch nor an ownership statement — "is now" between an old logo and a new one means a rename (现已更名为), "is now a product brand under X" is 现已成为 X 旗下的产品品牌, and 现已推出 is reserved for an actual NOW AVAILABLE product. Do not reduce a named platform to a tool either: where the copy calls the offering a 平台, "Analytics that deliver timely insights" is 提供及时洞察的分析平台, not 分析工具.',
		'Keep a neutral verb neutral and never rhetorically upgrade a flat one. "can significantly impact downtime, machine health and repairs" is 对停机、设备健康状况与维修产生显著影响 — never split it into 减少停机、改善健康、优化维修; "is a promise and our standard" is 既是承诺，也是我们的标准, not the 不仅……更是 escalation. Good copywriting that changes claim strength is still a fidelity error.',
		'Never downgrade a claim verb or swap a named capability for a neighbouring one. "predict failures" is 预测故障／预判故障 with the object kept, and 预警 is allowed only where the English says alert/warn/notify; 诊断 stays 诊断 (not 提示), 检测 stays 检测 (not 提醒). "collect, mine and measure data" is 采集、挖掘并测量数据 — rendering measure as 分析／衢量 silently replaces a named platform function with one already listed, and 测量 also matches the division name 测试与测量.',
		'Never change the noun a statistic counts, and give every counter its measure word. Countries stays 国家 (not 市场), people 人才／人员 (not 团队), locations 基地 (not 市场) — buyers put these numbers in comparison spreadsheets. Counter labels are numerals at runtime even though the HTML shows 0, so write 个国家, 名专业人才, 个全球基地, never the bare noun; "home countries" becomes the predicate 个国家设有本土团队. Getting three of four labels in a set right is the classic segment-by-segment signature.',
		'Priority and severity words stay inside their own tier and on their own axis, in plain functional register with no 成语: "non-urgent" is 非紧急, never 低优先级; "critical issue" is 严重故障, never 关键问题; "immediate safety risk" is 紧迫的安全风险, never 直接的安全风险. In an intake form this breaks routing and SLA, not just style.',
		'Keep every modifier and every relation the English states. Trailing purpose phrases survive ("for their consumers" = 为其消费者); an adverbial of duration attaches to the verb the English attaches it to ("Watch how we integrate X ... in a few minutes" is 用几分钟时间，观看我们如何将…集成…, never 观看我们如何在几分钟内将…, which claims the integration takes minutes); and the agent of a "for/from" noun phrase survives ("support requests for Bauer customers and other partners" means requests FROM them: Bauer 客户及其他合作伙伴提交的支持请求, not 对……的支持请求).',
		'Every Chinese verb needs its object, and every verb-object pair must be one that occurs in real Chinese industry writing. "allowing us to adapt swiftly" is 使我们能够迅速应变, never the objectless 迅速适应 — 适应、响应、提升、改善、满足 all require a stated object even where English drops it, and an English prepositional tail needs its own clause. Use 应对／迎接挑战 (never 解决挑战), 解决难题, 满足需求, 积累经验, 开展检测, 优化流程／配置 (never 优化需求), 汇聚人才／资源 (never 汇聚头脑); do not coordinate unlike categories under one verb just because English does; and a Chinese machine 做 a motion, it does not 执行 one.',
		'Never repeat the same morpheme inside one clause or label, and break a collision by changing the HEAD NOUN rather than the register. 无损检测 already IS non-destructive testing, so "NDT inspection" is 无损检测（NDT）, never 无损检测（NDT）检测; "Support & consulting sales inquiry" is 支持与咨询业务销售咨询, with the 销售咨询 suffix byte-identical across every sibling.',
		'Delete the second marker and the perfective 了 when the clause does not need them: 在故障发生前预警, never 在故障发生前提前预警 (same for 提前预先、事先预判、再次重复); "streamlines validation, improves throughput" is 简化验证流程、提高吞吐量, not 简化了…、提高了…, which reports a completed past event instead of a standing capability.',
		'Never open a Chinese sentence with a bare 或 copied from an English "Or ..." sentence — use 或者，… or fold the clause into the preceding sentence — and never open with a subjectless participial clause: "In a strategic move reflecting its commitment to X, Y announced…" is 作为一项战略举措，Y 宣布……，彰显其……的一贯承诺。 Split it; never stack the whole frame in front of 举措／方案／计划, and never turn it into a purpose clause with 为体现……, which converts substance into image management.',
		'Rewrite English word order into Chinese shape. Questions and headings go topic-comment: "How can we help you today?" is 今天我们能为您提供什么帮助？, "What\'s new at X?" is the noun phrase X 最新动态, "Searching <site>" labels a scope (在 <site> 中搜索, not 正在搜索). Job titles are strictly left-branching, department qualifier first: "Vice President of Global Sales, Aerospace & Industrials" is 航空航天与工业部门全球销售副总裁, and a place name inside a title stays a proper noun (Three Rivers 基地总经理). Degrees rebuild as 在<机构>取得<专业><学位> with established names (Master of Science in X = X 理学硕士), and a person takes a full Latin name on first mention then the established transliteration — never a bare Latin surname as the subject of a Chinese sentence.',
		'A one-word English nav category is often a clipped technical compound — expand it to the full Chinese industry term, and keep wayfinding labels plain and literal. In an HVAC/refrigeration menu "Climate & energy" is 暖通制冷与能源, never 气候与能源; "Power" in a driveline menu is 动力总成 and "Vision" in an inspection menu is 机器视觉; "Locations" is 全球基地, never 全球布局, which promises a strategy story and hides the address directory; "Industries served" is 覆盖行业, never bare 服务行业 (the service sector). Likewise when "machine" modifies data or analytics, translate the OBJECT: "machine health analytics" is 设备健康分析, because bare 机器分析 parses as mechanical analysis and hides the equipment-monitoring product.',
		'"Construction" as an activity is 施工／工程建设, not 建筑 (a building): "utilities construction" is 公用事业工程建设, because 公用事业建筑 narrows the claim to "utility buildings". "Affiliates" in a corporate footer means group companies, 关联公司, never 合作伙伴, which demotes a sister division to a third party. "Aftermarket" as a sales channel is 售后市场 everywhere; bare 售后 means after-sales service and cannot stand in for the channel.',
		'Read service-offer wording against the commercial model. "Contract balancing as-a-service" is 委托动平衡即服务（BaaS）, because 合同 is the paper contract and 合同动平衡 parses as "balancing of a contract", while unqualified "balancing-as-a-service" stays 动平衡即服务. "Gauging" in a capability list is dimensional gauging, 尺寸检测, never 测量, which flattens the term and collides with the division name 测试与测量. "Available X" in a menu of purchasable options goes predicate-final: 多种服务级别协议可选, not 可选服务级别协议 (readable as "the SLA is optional") and never 可用, which misparses as an availability (uptime) SLA.',
		'Keep the engineering colour of a verb used by an engineering company, and use a neutral adverb for corporate capability. "we engineer new possibilities" is 我们以工程之力开创新的可能, never bare 开创／打造; "from the team that builds the test systems" is 由打造这些测试系统的团队直接提供, never 亲自提供, and never 倾情、用心、贴心 in B2B equipment copy. Keep register plain and industrial: "sharp minds" is 顶尖人才, because 汇聚 collocates with 人才, never 头脑. Never translate a hortative CTA with 让我们 plus a verb — no Chinese CTA uses that calque: "Let\'s talk" is 洽谈合作, "Let\'s get started" is 立即开始, "Join us" is 加入我们, and if a sibling already renders 联系我们 for "Contact us", pick the other option so two different English CTAs stay distinct.',
		'Form microcopy is written as native Chinese UI, not as translated English sentences. A <select> placeholder "Select an option" is 请选择 (never 选择一个选项); "Any error codes from the system you can share?" is 可否提供系统报出的错误代码？; "select from the forms below" keeps the choosing, 从下方选择相应表单填写, never 填写下方表单, which erases the routing instruction on a page with several form tabs. In a chat or contact widget "message" is 消息, never 信息, and every placeholder takes 请 plus a verb (请输入您的姓名).',
		'Translate EVERY string a consent/cookie component prints from its config payload, not only the banner sentences: table headers (名称／域名／有效期), count words (项 Cookie), the Privacy Policy link label, every aria-label (Cookie consent → Cookie 同意设置), the cross-border transfer disclosure, and the durations in Chinese units (2 年, 30 分钟, 3 个月, session = 会话期间). A Chinese dialog wrapped around an English table is the most visible half-translation on the site, and it is the panel PIPL-minded legal and procurement readers open. The controls themselves go verb-first: "Google Analytics Opt Out" is 退出 Google Analytics 跟踪, "Manage cookie preferences" is 管理 Cookie 偏好设置 (设置, not 控制), never ending a clickable label with a trailing 选择退出, and a user instruction stays imperative: "Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information" is 请勿出售或分享我的个人信息, not the flat 不出售或分享….',
		'aria-label navigation landmarks name the region, not the English adjective: "Primary" is 主导航, "Mobile primary" is 移动端主导航 — never 主要, never 移动端优先 (the mobile-first design philosophy); any one-word landmark label takes 导航 as its head noun.',
		'Named offerings are brands even when every word looks translatable. If a phrase is a product or service name in a nav, footer product column or menu card (ADAS Garage, XL Machine, Burke Porter, Cimat, Galileo, Lismar, Titan, Kleinknecht, WinterPark, Bauer, Sentia, Ascentialytics, Ascential Care), keep the WHOLE name in Latin script. Never half-translate a brand in one place and keep it in another on the same page, never attach ™ to a translated phrase, and when a label wraps a brand in <span class="tmm-brand-word">, ONLY the brand belongs inside that span.',
		'Use Simplified characters (简体), never Traditional, and full-width punctuation inside every Chinese sentence: ，。、；：？！, curly quotes “ ” and （） — even when the English source shows ASCII " \' ( ). Half-width characters appear only inside an untranslated Latin run. Use full-width ／ for every slash inside Chinese copy (轻微磨损／损伤) and 《》 for a document title before 白皮书.',
		'Insert a single half-width space only where real Latin text or digits sit next to Chinese (使用 API 接口) — never around an inline <span> or <a> inside a Chinese sentence (将一切<span>集成</span>在一起) and never between two Chinese characters.',
		'Numbers use Western digits (1,500), with 万 and 亿 for large quantities where natural; currency ¥1,500 or 1,500 元; dates YYYY 年 MM 月 DD 日 (2026 年 9 月 22 日) or YYYY-MM-DD, one convention per list; 24-hour time (14:30). Never change a magnitude or a unit the English states.',
	),
	'avoid' => array(
		'Traditional Chinese characters when targeting Mainland China.',
